WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.402 --> 00:00:02.985
Unit eighteen. Menstrual Health!

2
00:00:03.907 --> 00:00:07.376
Hello, everyone! I'm Doctor Visal, your school doctor.

3
00:00:07.426 --> 00:00:10.465
Hi, Doctor Visal! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:10.515 --> 00:00:13.767
Today we learn about Menstrual Health. Let's go!

5
00:00:14.704 --> 00:00:18.487
Menstruation. Say it with me. Menstruation!

6
00:00:22.045 --> 00:00:25.478
Cycle. Say it with me. Cycle!

7
00:00:28.949 --> 00:00:31.832
Pad. Say it with me. Pad!

8
00:00:35.323 --> 00:00:38.556
Hygiene. Say it with me. Hygiene!

9
00:00:42.029 --> 00:00:45.396
Cramps. Say it with me. Cramps!

10
00:00:48.929 --> 00:00:51.929
Iron. Say it with me. Iron!

11
00:00:55.434 --> 00:00:58.550
Stigma. Say it with me. Stigma!

12
00:01:02.091 --> 00:01:05.191
Support. Say it with me. Support!

13
00:01:08.656 --> 00:01:18.447
Menstruation is part of a healthy monthly cycle. Good hygiene includes changing pads regularly. Iron-rich food helps, and there should be no stigma — everyone can offer support.

14
00:01:18.497 --> 00:01:21.332
Now I understand. Thank you, Doctor Visal!

15
00:01:22.924 --> 00:01:27.945
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:27.995 --> 00:01:29.133
Pad!

17
00:01:29.904 --> 00:01:34.975
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:35.025 --> 00:01:36.175
Stigma!

19
00:01:36.988 --> 00:01:44.955
Did you know? A menstrual cycle usually lasts about 21–35 days in adults and can be irregular at first for teens!

20
00:01:45.005 --> 00:01:47.034
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:47.787 --> 00:01:55.762
Think and answer. How can schools support students during their periods?

22
00:01:55.812 --> 00:01:56.962
Great answer!

23
00:01:57.937 --> 00:02:02.427
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:02.477 --> 00:02:04.940
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

